<task id="093" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Two server defects found diagnosing UAT-9: a saved document's job row never reaches a terminal state, and `using var activity = Activity.Current` (20 sites) ends the request's own trace span early</title>
    <phase>6 UAT round 3 (2026-10-03)</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF `.cs` in `Workers/Office` and the shared `Infrastructure/Graph`, adds a guard test.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>(B) is mechanical with a guard; (A) needs a root-cause trace (why three rows closed and five did not) before any change — hence xhigh.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>UAT3-W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Wave W2 with 089 (client-only, runs no `dotnet`). Server-only: 093 is the only W2 task that builds the BFF. `Infrastructure/Graph` is shared with other projects — run `/conflict-check` first.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>088</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, jobs, telemetry, observability, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Two defects found while diagnosing owner UAT-9 on 2026-10-03, recorded in `notes/042-uat-round3-2026-10-03.md` §4. Owner rule of 2026-09-21: every finding is fixed in this project.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE BFF developer: Office save pipeline (ADR-004 jobs, ADR-017 job status) and OpenTelemetry/Azure Monitor tracing.</role>

  <goal>(A) Every Office save's `sprk_processingjob` row ends in a terminal state that tells the truth about the pipeline; (B) request telemetry for every Graph-touching route reports its real status code and duration.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - **(A) Evidence (dev, 2026-10-02/03)**: every successful save since 10-02 20:49 (5 of 5) left its row at
        `sprk_status = 1`, `sprk_currentstage = FileUploaded`, `sprk_progress = 70`. Three saves on 10-02 at 12:22,
        12:25 and 13:27 ended `2 / Complete / 100`. In the 17:03 save the request logged
        `recorded: Completed, Complete, 100%` (the save's own view, stored in `sprk_result`, which the pane reads —
        **the pane is not affected**); about 1 s later `UploadFinalizationWorker` wrote Running/`FileUploaded`/70
        (`UploadFinalizationWorker.cs` Step 9) and `QueueNextStageAsync` (`:826`) handed profiling to
        `AppOnlyDocumentAnalysis` and RAG indexing to their own jobs, which do not know the Office job id. Nothing
        closes the row. When `TriggerAiProcessing` is false the worker marks it Completed (`:353+`) — check whether
        that explains the midday rows.
      - **The row's meaning** (`OfficeJobStatusService.cs` header, task 060): `sprk_result` = the SAVE (pane);
        `sprk_status`/`sprk_currentstage`/`sprk_progress` = the PIPELINE. Profiling and indexing have their own
        outcome columns on the document (`sprk_filesummarystatus`, `sprk_searchindexed`).
      - **(B) Evidence**: `UploadSessionManager.cs:122` `using var activity = Activity.Current;` disposes the REQUEST's
        Activity when `UploadSmallAsync` returns. The request is then exported early: `resultCode 0`, `success false`,
        1.4 s of a 3 s request, carrying the upload's tags (`operation=UploadSmall`, `driveId`, `filePath`). Both
        "status 0" saves on 10-03 (16:48, 17:03) succeeded. The same line is at **20 sites**:
        `DriveItemOperations.cs` ×15, `ContainerOperations.cs` ×4, `UploadSessionManager.cs` ×1 (grep
        `using\s+var\s+\w+\s*=\s*Activity\.Current`).
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-017">(A) The pipeline's terminal state must be persisted. Choose ONE owner of "pipeline finished" and state why. Preferred unless the trace shows otherwise: the finalization worker marks the row Completed once the follow-on jobs are queued (stage naming what was queued), because profiling and indexing already persist their own outcomes on the document; do NOT thread the Office job id into the shared `AppOnlyDocumentAnalysis` handler unless the trace proves it is the only correct owner.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 060">(A) Do not change `sprk_result` or what the pane reads; the save's own view stays exactly as it is.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">(B) Do not dispose an Activity this code did not start. Either drop `using` (tags then go on the current span, as today, minus the early stop) or start a real child span from an `ActivitySource`; pick one for all 20 sites and state why. Behaviour of the Graph calls is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">(B) Add a guard that fails the build when `using` is applied to `Activity.Current` anywhere under `src/server` (an ArchTests source-scan test, the repo's existing pattern for text guards); seed it by reverting one site and watching it fail.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Publish size vs a FRESH master build (Compress-Archive, equal file counts); CVE check; `/conflict-check` before editing `Infrastructure/Graph`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">(A) test in the existing `UploadFinalizationWorker` test class; (B) the ArchTests guard. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">(A) The note states, from the code, why the 10-02 midday rows closed and the later ones did not.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(A) A successful save with AI processing ends with its row in a terminal status (Completed) and a stage that names what was handed on; a finalization failure ends Failed; a test pins both. `sprk_result` is byte-identical before/after for the same save.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(B) No `using` on `Activity.Current` remains under `src/server`; the guard test fails when one is reintroduced (seeded) and passes otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(B) A test proves the request Activity is still running after `UploadSmallAsync` returns (e.g. an `ActivityListener` sees no Stop for the parent before the caller stops it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: BFF Office test scope, the Graph infrastructure tests and ArchTests green; publish delta reported vs fresh master; CVE clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Live (after a deploy): a Word save's request shows its real status (202) and full duration in App Insights, and its job row reads Completed. If no deploy is available, leave open and say so.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The trace shows a consumer that relies on the row staying non-terminal (e.g. a monitor or reconciliation job reading `sprk_status` = In Progress) — STOP and report before changing it.</trigger>
    <trigger>`/conflict-check` reports another active project editing `Infrastructure/Graph/DriveItemOperations.cs` or `ContainerOperations.cs` — coordinate before editing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>`/conflict-check`; read the worker, `OfficeJobStatusService`, and the 20 sites.</step>
    <step>(A) Root cause from the code; choose the owner; fix; tests.</step>
    <step>(B) Fix all 20 sites one way; the Activity test; the ArchTests guard, seeded.</step>
    <step>Gates and publish size; record in `notes/093-job-row-and-telemetry.md`; TASK-INDEX 093 → done.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>The finalization worker, the job status service and the Graph operations exist; ArchTests already hosts source-scan guards.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — fixes inside existing classes plus one guard test; no new service or route.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every saved document's job looks stuck forever (ADR-017's persisted outcome is false), and App Insights reports successful saves and file operations as failures with wrong durations, hiding real ones.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

